# id  tag  kind  t_s  alt_km  L_si_W  flag  note
1 - first_light 0.0030 100.000 4.7844e+04 info  L_si first exceeds 1e-6 of its peak. This is just a visibility threshold; the real value depends on your sensor floor and on where the simulation starts (zstart).
2 A ablation_onset 1.4970 80.592 1.4394e+06 stylized  Net heating flux first exceeds radiative loss at T_ablate = 2300 K, so ablation switches on (a kink in the slope). Real onset is gradual over a few km. BELOW this point the model's light is drag work only (no ablated material): treat light above ~81 km as low-confidence. Loosely like the end of Phase 1 / start of Phase 2 in [R22], but the model has no spin, volatile (Na/K) emission or melt physics.
3 Y first_yield 3.3060 57.093 7.9002e+07 physical  Loading rho v^2 reaches S0 = 0.1 MPa. The body starts to flatten (pancake): area, drag and heating all grow, so the light rises faster. Analogue of the onset of fragmentation (Phase 5 / H_f in [R22]).
4 F flare 3.4209 55.601 2.3598e+08 stylized  Light rises x17.2 in 0.29 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: yield gen 0 at 57.1 km (100% of m0); split gen 0 at 54.3 km (100% of m0). Dust groups supply 75% of the rise and 71% of the light at the end of the flare. A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
5 B first_breakup 3.5190 54.328 5.1441e+08 stylized  Spread factor reached f_split = 2: the body breaks into 4 children plus 20 % of its mass as dust. The dust has a large area-to-mass ratio, decelerates and ablates within a fraction of a second, which makes a sharp flare. The instantaneous release is a model simplification. Light grew x6.5 between first yield and this breakup (pancake spreading).
6 - drag_overtakes_ablation 4.4190 42.900 3.3215e+09 stylized  Drag work now exceeds the kinetic energy carried off by ablated mass. The ratio ablation/drag is about Lambda v^2/(2 Q Cd), so this happens when the speed falls below ~14 km/s (from the model's heating law).
7 F flare 4.7496 38.690 7.9730e+09 stylized  Light rises x3.4 in 0.14 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: yield gen 1 at 38.9 km (36% of m0); yield gen 1 at 38.9 km (18% of m0); yield gen 1 at 38.9 km (12% of m0) +5 more. Dust groups supply 38% of the rise and 40% of the light at the end of the flare. A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
8 F flare 5.0144 35.390 1.6302e+10 stylized  Light rises x1.6 in 0.11 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: yield gen 2 at 35.6 km (12% of m0); yield gen 2 at 35.5 km (6% of m0); yield gen 2 at 35.5 km (4% of m0) +5 more. Dust groups supply 0% of the rise and 21% of the light at the end of the flare. A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
9 P peak 5.0513 34.937 2.1536e+10 physical  Maximum light. It sits ~+0.7 km from the peak of energy deposition (34.2 km) because the luminous efficiency tau(v) falls as the fragments slow (mass-weighted speed here 12.9 km/s).
10 D rolloff 5.2823 32.627 7.8797e+09 physical  Light has fallen to 1/e of the peak 0.23 s after it. Cause: the kinetic energy is being used up (speed 72% of v0, 58% of the mass still in flight) and tau(v) drops with speed. Analogue of Phase 7 (decline until dark flight) in [R22].
11 b bump 5.3249 32.155 8.5483e+09 stylized  Small fluctuation, 6% above the local trend; coincides with a yield (gen 2) at 31.9 km. The fine structure of this phase is set by the cascade rules, so its pattern is not predictive of a real event.
12 R retirement_step 6.3853 25.683 5.5063e+07 artifact  A group is removed because it slowed below v_dark = 3.0 km/s; the light drops 17% within 0.03 s. A bookkeeping step, not a physical dimming.
13 R retirement_step 6.4183 25.555 4.4806e+07 artifact  A group is removed because it slowed below v_dark = 3.0 km/s; the light drops 18% within 0.03 s. A bookkeeping step, not a physical dimming.
14 R retirement_step 6.4393 25.457 3.8988e+07 artifact  A group is removed because it slowed below v_dark = 3.0 km/s; the light drops 18% within 0.03 s. A bookkeeping step, not a physical dimming.
15 R retirement_step 6.4663 25.356 3.2554e+07 artifact  A group is removed because it slowed below v_dark = 3.0 km/s; the light drops 18% within 0.03 s. A bookkeeping step, not a physical dimming.
16 T tail 6.5263 25.141 2.1329e+07 low-confidence  Below 1e-3 of the peak the light is controlled by groups being retired when they slow below v_dark = 3.0 km/s and by the tau taper (2-4 km/s). Do not interpret structure below this level.
17 R retirement_step 6.8083 24.296 2.4266e+06 artifact  A group is removed because it slowed below v_dark = 3.0 km/s; the light drops 22% within 0.03 s. A bookkeeping step, not a physical dimming.
